      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-05-25_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <head>Examiners Saturday, May 25, 1907</head>
        <p>The Examiners Saturday, May 25, 1907</p>
        <p>2 'AAP McDOUGALL'S Patelit SELF-RAISING FLOUR THETIM</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON FOOTBALL CLUB.</p>
        <p>fair treatment. On the first occasion on which they won the trophy they did not give Berry a medal, with the result that they lost his servicn for half a season.</p>
        <p>Mr. ASHTON said a serious principle was involved, During the past season they were fortunate in going through the cup ties with only three reserve men, while next season they might have to play eight or ten extra men, and if they had to present every man who took part in one cup tie with Ei medal it would be an expen- sive matter.</p>
        <p>The PRESIDENT ruled the discussion ont of order. BENEFIT MATCH FOR ISHERWOOD.</p>
        <p>Mr. H. ROGERS asked if anything had been done towards giving 'lsherwood a beneat match. He thought Isherwood was entitled to one. , The PRESIDENT said nothing had been done, but if anything was suggested the committee would take it into consideration.</p>
        <p>Mr. ROGERS then suggested the matter, and the PRESIDENT, amidst applause, said it would be considered</p>
        <p>HONORARIUMS. On the proposition of Mr. DuTrox, seconded by Mr. OsBORNE, it was decided ,to present the usual honorariums to the Secretary, Treasurer and Auditors. MEMENTO OF THE CUP VICTORY.</p>
        <p>It was decided on the proposition of M. LISTER, seconded by Mr. ENGLAND, to present the President and Messrs. Chalmers and Barber with rings, as a memento of the cup victory, Mr. LAster remarking that all the other officials had h3,d rings presented to them when the team won the cup two years ago. When the matter was introduced Mr. CIiA.LMBRS said that as a mattet of principle he objected.</p>
