al value of £7O coming to the "good old town." Warrington friends of Mr. Lowe will congratulate him In addition Messrs. frosfield's band seoured two upon his success. awards at Darwen on Saturday. The heartiest con- gratulations are due to the winners and we hope this The Ship Canal Bill. . musical enthusiasm and friendly rivalry will long con- , This measure comes before a committee of the House !of foramens on Tuesday next. Opposition will- be tinue to bring honour to Warrington. * ~., * forthcoming from Warrington Corporation and Spontaneity is the great charm of the essay, the traders on the question of the increased salinity of charm which gives Charles Lamb his value and is the river which it is contended might result,all other worth more to Steele even than his exquisite sense of points in dispute having been settled. form. No one will imagine that spontaneity is incom- patible with hard work; but the most important work ' Above all Wear BA.NK.I'S HATS and CAPS.—Advt. 4 is done not on the essay, but on the mind that con- ' LADIES' BEST GLACE BOOTS AND SHOES, UNDER ceives it. Make yourself as wise and as witty and as ; THE CLOCK, BRIDGE-STREET.—Adtv. learned as you can, and the essay will look after. Beautiful Warrington Society. 'I itself. There is no form of literature that depends so . - much on the personality, the character and the attain- The third distributian of the season took place on ; Saturday last at the Depat, Factory-lane, about 20 meats of the author.—." The Academy." C , * ! members participating. The lots : distributed, about The Railway Institute as made great headway 'lOO ix' number, included iris, phlox (red and white), during the first year of its existence, and a most London pride, delphinium, ex-eye-daisy, polyanthus, satisfactory state of affairs was reviewed at the annual thrift, lupin, stocks, asters, dwarf French marigold, meeting. i Mr. I. T. Williams, whose departure for lobelia (blue and white). The next distribution which London