        <p>LIGHTS OUT.</p>
        <p>An old Highland sergeant in one of the Scot- tish regiments was going on his rounds one night to see that things were all right, particularly to make sure that the lights wen out in the barrack rooms. Coming to a roc,:. where he thought he saw a liht,phining, he shouted out, "Put out that light there!" One of the men called back: "It's the moon, ser- geant!" Not hearing very well, the serge:l cried in returns "I don't care a button what is; put it out 1"</p>
